This scale drawing of a car park uses a scale of $1:500$.
Find the real length of the car park, in metres.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (4,2.2);
\node[below] at (2,0) {$8\text{ cm}$};
\node at (2,1.1) {Car park};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

On this scale drawing of a yard, the $3$ cm fence represents a real length of $6$ m. Find the real length of the $7$ cm fence, in metres.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (4.2,1.8);
\node[below] at (2.1,0) {$7\text{ cm}$};
\node[left] at (0,0.9) {$3\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
